{
  "$comment": [
    "Expected-code metadata for the cross-rule determinism gate",
    "(CG-0MWSJYY9S0046V55). Tests do not hard-code the corpus: this file is the",
    "single table the sweep reads, so adding or renaming a fixture without",
    "declaring what it must report is a gate failure.",
    "",
    "`corpus` lists every committed manifest fixture in this directory and the",
    "exact findings the CLI must emit for it when bound to the shipped",
    "long-erasure.csv. The expectations are THE CLI's, not the per-rule unit",
    "tests' (those validate without content bound); a bound fixture may cascade",
    "into a second rule by design, and the cascade is pinned here so a rule",
    "cannot become unreachable, or newly reachable, unnoticed.",
    "",
    "`contentOverrides` covers the rule families whose defect cannot be expressed",
    "as a manifest-only mutation (the failing input lives in the content file).",
    "Both mutations are applied to the shipped rows exactly as written and written",
    "to a temp file, so the sweep still goes through the CLI's real --content path.",
    "",
    "G10 (CG-0MWR0BJXI007UINE) retired the legacy `clockCost` CSV column, so the",
    "migration-only `clock-cost-mismatch` rule never runs and no corpus entry",
    "expects it. The retired code stays in the §2.4 union by design."
  ],
  "manifest": "example-games/gym/content/long-erasure-episode.json",
  "content": "example-games/gym/content/long-erasure.csv",
  "corpus": [
    {
      "file": "cards-dangling-chain.json",
